FINAL ANSWER:
## 🚌 lib/ bus factor: **1**

Period: all history. Generated 2026-10-23. Scope is `lib/`, which holds one file: `lib/index.js` (238 lines). That file is the package entry point (`"main": "./lib/index.js"`), so the whole `cors` package depends on it.

**Answer:** one person has to leave before nobody understands it. That person is **Troy Goode**.

---

### Raw blame is misleading

Run plain `git blame` and **Fiona Formatter** owns 214 of 238 lines (90%). That comes from one commit, `62628c0 style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes` (2026-04-12). It changed indentation and quotes and nothing else. I re-ran blame without that commit and with whitespace ignored (`git blame -w --ignore-rev 62628c0`):

| Author | Lines (real) | % | Commits | Last commit to lib |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 159 | **67%** | 29 / 61 | 2026-04-10 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 22 | 9% | 4 | 2017-10 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (and alias `alex94puchades`) | 16 | 7% | 5 | 2015-05 |
| Raymond Feng | 7 | 3% | 1 | 2015-01 |
| 15 others | 34 | 14% | 1–3 each | 2013–2021 |
| Fiona Formatter | 0 | 0% | 1 (formatting only) | 2026-04-12 |

### Why the answer is 1

- If Troy leaves, the people left own 33% of the logic. That is below the 50% threshold.
- Everyone else in the table last touched `lib/` between 2013 and 2021, so their knowledge of it is 5–13 years old.
- Only two people have committed to `lib/` in the past year: Troy (real change) and Fiona (formatting only).
- No one has committed to `lib/` in the last 90 days. The last commit was 2026-04-12, about 6 months ago. Troy is "active" only in the sense that he committed this year.

| Metric | Value |
|---|---|
| Files analyzed | 1 |
| Bus factor | 1 |
| Primary owner | Troy Goode (67% of lines, 47% of commits) |
| Dependents | The whole package (it is the entry point) |
| Risk | 🔴 **CRITICAL** |

```
lib/
└── index.js  [██████████] 🔴 Bus Factor: 1 (Troy Goode 67%; no other active owner)
```

### Mitigating factor

The rest of the repo had other active contributors in the past year: Jon Church, Ignacio Mangas, Ulises Gascón, Phillip Barta and Vansh Sharma. None of them changed `lib/`, but they could take it over. The file is also small (238 lines) and has tests (`test/`), so someone new could learn it quickly.

### Recommendations

1. **Immediate:** have one of the active maintainers (Jon Church or Ulises Gascón) review Troy's next changes to `lib/index.js`, or pair with Troy on them.
2. **Short-term:** add a `.git-blame-ignore-revs` file that lists `62628c0`. Without it, blame and ownership tools (and GitHub's blame view) will keep showing Fiona Formatter as the owner.
3. **Ongoing:** document the option-handling and preflight logic in `lib/index.js`, and require a second reviewer for changes to `lib/`.

